get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/project/getProjectBySlug/{{projectSlug}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  # Get Project By Slug

  Public. This is what `/projects/[slug]` on the website calls — **Get Project**
  stays for the dashboard's edit page, which holds an id.

  A separate route rather than one param that accepts either: `getProjectById`
  validates its param as an ObjectId, so a slug sent there is rejected with 422.

  Slugs are derived from the title at create time and never move on their own —
  renaming a project leaves its URL alone. An admin can still set the slug
  explicitly, and the old ObjectId URL keeps working: the website redirects it
  permanently to the slug.

  | Status | Meaning |
  | --- | --- |
  | 200 | the full project, including `projectDetails` |
  | 404 | `NOT_FOUND` |
  | 422 | `VALIDATION_ERROR` — not a lowercase, dash-separated slug |
}
